# THE FOUNDER BOOK — how many accounts the supplier launches holding.
#
# R13 CURRICULUM, DIRECTOR-DECIDED. Read by `simulation/live_population.py` on every run. This
# file, not the code, sets the number. The baseline world (real 2016-25 history, externally
# calibrated generators) is untouched by it: what changes is which world the company lives
# through, which is the director's and is named and versioned here.
#
# THE DECISION
#   Director, 2026-08-28, verbatim: "take the 80 founders -- that's my answer on P9".
#   Priced menu: docs/staging/SEAT_TO_DIRECTOR_P9_BOOK_DEPTH_PRICED_2026-08-28.md
#   Question it answers: P9 of DIRECTOR_GUIDANCE_THE_WORLD_MUST_PRESS_2026-08-28 --
#     "Only 37 accounts carry five or more renewals, so nothing can compound. Book depth
#      bounds every comparison."
#
# WHY IT IS A CURRICULUM ACT AND NOT A FIDELITY ONE. A supplier that launches by acquiring a
# portfolio and then grows organically is an ordinary GB shape, so neither 13 nor 80 is more
# faithful than the other. What the number decides is what the machine can be ASKED: at 13
# founders no per-customer pricing policy has anything to compound on, and three separate
# instruments hit that same wall on 2026-08-28 -- the price ladder's 17 binary decisions, the
# chase-on/chase-off comparison, and A48's method skill on 12 decisions across 5 accounts.
#
# WHAT IT COSTS, recorded because a curriculum act should carry its price:
#   * WIDTH. The customer-year budget is fixed, so founders are paid for out of growth. The
#     book falls from ~264 accounts to ~180, and the acquisition funnel's ~241 wins to ~100.
#     The growth story gets quieter; that trade is the reason the decision was the director's.
#   * WALL CLOCK. None. Same budget, same settle time, same publish cadence.
#   * EVERY PUBLISHED FIGURE MOVES. A different book is a different supplier. Comparisons
#     across this boundary are comparisons of two books and must say so.
#
# REVERTING: set `founder_accounts` back to `13` (the hand-authored roster alone) or delete this
# file -- `founder_book()` falls back to the static roster and the run is the pre-decision one.
# A malformed or out-of-range value is IGNORED with the fallback kept, never read as zero: a
# YAML typo must not silently empty the opening book.

version: 1
decided_on: "2026-08-28"
decided_by: director

#: Accounts the supplier holds on day one of the window. The hand-authored roster (13, serving)
#: is INCLUDED in this count, not added to it, so the number here is the whole opening book and
#: a reader does not have to know the roster's size to know what was chosen.
founder_accounts: 80

#: Bounds. Below the roster's own size the number cannot be honoured (the roster cannot be
#: shrunk by this file); above the customer-year budget it would leave no growth at all, which
#: is Option 4 of the priced menu and was not chosen.
min_founder_accounts: 13
max_founder_accounts: 120
